      "code": "g9u8.r.05",
      "volume": "9",
      "unit": "U8",
      "genre": "议论文",
      "title": "Making Guesses",
      "body": "In daily life, we often make guesses about things we are not sure of. We use special words to show how sure we are. If we are very sure, we use \"must\". For example, if the lights are on, someone must be home. If we are less sure, we use \"might\" or \"could\". The keys might be in the kitchen, or they could be in the car. If we think something is impossible, we use \"can't\". A small cat can't make such a loud sound. Making guesses is a useful skill. It helps us understand the world around us. But we should remember that a guess is not always right.",
      "word_count": 110,
      "difficulty": 3,
      "vocab_notes": [
